  "dataset_path": "protocol/asn/sample-asn.tsv",
  "description": "Shared first-attempt prevention vectors. Each row pins the trusted-history state the engine evaluates an AuthenticationSuccess against; the expected block carries one cell per novelty enforcement mode. The F16 core is the cross product of the binary history axes (asn seen or unseen, prefix seen or new, device continuity bound or unbound) over the two modes; the remaining rows pin the dataset-less ASN fallback (where the account trusted axis decides), the seen but untrusted continuity trap, scope pressure, the breached credential flag, the fail-closed probe outage, and the non-login event. Every request carries one session pseudonym and one device pseudonym; only the session tag is ever seeded, so the post-call device trust reads as the binding detector. Trust is sticky in the canonical store: a record without the trust flag never revokes a minted mirror. Both the Rust suite (packages/kiwicaptcha-risk/tests/first_attempt_vectors.rs) and the PHP mirror (FirstAttemptVectorsTest.php) consume this corpus.",
